What is Thread Safety?
Interview Definition

Thread Safety means multiple threads can access and modify shared data correctly 
without causing inconsistent or unexpected results.

===============================================================================
Real-Life Example

Imagine you and your friend have a bank account.

Current Balance:

₹1000

Both of you try to withdraw:

₹500

at exactly the same time.

Case 1 - Without Thread Safety
Balance = ₹1000

Thread 1 checks:

Balance = ₹1000

Thread 2 also checks:

Balance = ₹1000

Both think money is available.

Both withdraw ₹500.

Sometimes the balance becomes incorrect because both threads read and update the shared data simultaneously.

This is a Race Condition.

Case 2 - With Thread Safety

Thread 1:

Checks Balance

↓

Withdraws

↓

Updates Balance

↓

Releases Lock

Only then...

Thread 2 starts.

Now the balance remains correct.
